the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the person id of the parameters is *a text*.
    the benefit of the parameters is *a text*.
    the check result is *a truth value*.

the templates are:
    the enrollments of the situation include *a person id* with *a benefit*.
    the enrollments of the situation are listed.

the knowledge base person_enrolled_in_benefit includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/person-enrolled-in-benefit.dmn".

rule check_result_1 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is true if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
    and the person id is equal to the person id of the parameters
    and the benefit is equal to the benefit of the parameters.

rule check_result_2 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is false if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the person id of the parameters is a text
    and the benefit of the parameters is a second text
    and it is not the case that
        the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
        and the person id of the parameters is a third text
        and the person id is equal to the third text
        and the benefit of the parameters is a fourth text
        and the benefit is equal to the fourth text.

scenario Enrollments_empty is, as stated in the Bruno requests of PersonEnrolledInBenefit at test case Enrollments empty:
    the benefit of the parameters is "bogus".
    the person id of the parameters is "p1".
    the enrollments of the situation are listed.
    q_d_check_result expects answers ["the check result is false"].

scenario Enrollments_null is, as stated in the Bruno requests of PersonEnrolledInBenefit at test case Enrollments null:
    the benefit of the parameters is "bogus".
    the person id of the parameters is "p1".
    q_d_check_result expects answers [].

query q_d_check_result is:
    the check result is which truth value.

